aira-forecaster-agents
# ...except the tax reference tables. They contain no user data and no proprietary
# logic, and keeping them untracked meant a correction on one machine never reached
# the other two — RMD_TABLES.md carried a wrong age-89 divisor (13.0 vs the IRS 12.9)
# on 2 of 3 machines while CLAUDE.md calls these files the canonical source. That is a
# live trap: the next person to port doc values into code introduces a real RMD bug.
!aira-forecaster-agents/
!aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/
!aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/TAX_REFERENCE.md
!aira-forecaster-agents/knowledge/RMD_TABLES.md

# Markdown docs — only README tracked (CLAUDE.md is private, synced manually)
*.md
!README.md

# Local/integration tests — never commit
*.local.js
*.local.ts
TEST_REPORT.md
tests/local/

